%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 077672a9565156242a921fb3d20dae3f, type: 3}
  m_Name: OpenHousePlanningMeeting
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HomeTasks::HomeTasks.MeetingContent
  meetingTitle: Open House Planning
  recording: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 04d09ab8ededa1440a9b0ca60c0be023, type: 3}
  captions:
  - startTime: 0
    endTime: 4
    text: Hello, everyone. Can you hear me clearly?
  - startTime: 4
    endTime: 9
    text: Today we're going to plan our company's open house.
  - startTime: 9
    endTime: 14
    text: We'll focus on the poster and publicity.
  - startTime: 14
    endTime: 18
    text: We'll also cover registration. Let's finalize the plan today.
  - startTime: 18
    endTime: 25
    text: Let's agree who's responsible for each part and when it's due, so everyone
      can plan their time.
  - startTime: 25
    endTime: 28
    text: Let's start with the event details.
  - startTime: 28
    endTime: 32
    text: Our open house will be on December 21.
  - startTime: 32
    endTime: 37
    text: It runs from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. on the second floor of the activity building.
  - startTime: 37
    endTime: 44.8
    text: We originally planned to use Room 201, but we've moved to Room 203.
  - startTime: 44.8
    endTime: 48.8
    text: The air conditioner in the original room is being repaired.
  - startTime: 48.8
    endTime: 54
    text: Please use the new room number in all the documents and publicity.
  - startTime: 54
    endTime: 61
    text: May sent me the poster yesterday. I've checked it, and it looks good overall.
  - startTime: 61
    endTime: 65
    text: The main image and headline are clear.
  - startTime: 65
    endTime: 69
    text: We need to update the room number and the registration wording.
  - startTime: 69
    endTime: 74
    text: "Use the wording \u201CRegister in advance to reserve a seat.\u201D"
  - startTime: 74
    endTime: 80
    text: Put the QR code at the bottom and leave some space around it.
  - startTime: 80
    endTime: 85.5
    text: That way, people can easily scan it with their phones.
  - startTime: 86
    endTime: 93
    text: Next is the registration form. Ton will take care of it.
  - startTime: 93
    endTime: 98
    text: Collect each person's name, email, and the activity they'd like to join.
  - startTime: 98
    endTime: 106
    text: We have three workshop sessions, each with room for about 20 people.
  - startTime: 106
    endTime: 113
    text: When a session fills up, update the form so people can only choose sessions
      with space.
  - startTime: 113
    endTime: 122
    text: People who only want to see the exhibition can walk in and register on-site.
  - startTime: 122
    endTime: 126
    text: Okay, let's go over the deadlines.
  - startTime: 126
    endTime: 134
    text: Ton, please send me the form link and QR code by noon tomorrow.
  - startTime: 134
    endTime: 142
    text: May, add the code to the poster and send the revised version to the group
      by 4 p.m. tomorrow.
  - startTime: 142
    endTime: 148
    text: We'll check everything for accuracy on Thursday morning.
  - startTime: 148
    endTime: 157.7
    text: We'll schedule it to go live on the website around 10 a.m. on Friday so
      it's on time.
  - startTime: 158.3
    endTime: 166
    text: Before publishing, make sure the latest file is in the shared folder.
  - startTime: 166
    endTime: 171
    text: Pay particular attention to the date, time, venue, and QR code.
  - startTime: 171
    endTime: 174
    text: If something needs fixing, leave a comment in that same file.
  - startTime: 174
    endTime: 178
    text: May will gather the feedback and make the edits.
  - startTime: 178.5
    endTime: 185
    text: Let's also talk about the event photos we'll use in the post.
  - startTime: 185
    endTime: 192
    text: Could the venue team take photos of Room 203 from two or three angles?
  - startTime: 192
    endTime: 199
    text: Show the entrance and the space for the table so the team can plan the
      registration area.
  - startTime: 199
    endTime: 204
    text: We'll set up the registration table outside the room.
  - startTime: 204
    endTime: 212
    text: Staff should arrive at 8 a.m. to set up the equipment and start welcoming
      attendees.
  - startTime: 212
    endTime: 217
    text: Now, I'd like you to do the final check on the poster.
  - startTime: 217
    endTime: 220
    text: Check the date, time, and room number.
  - startTime: 220
    endTime: 225
    text: Scan the QR code to make sure the full registration form opens.
  - startTime: 225
    endTime: 231
    text: If everything is in order, let the group know by 11 a.m. tomorrow.
  - startTime: 231
    endTime: 235
    text: Before we wrap up, I have a few questions for you.
  - startTime: 235
    endTime: 239
    text: Which room should the latest poster list?
  - startTime: 239
    endTime: 241.6
    text: What do you need to check?
  - startTime: 241.6
    endTime: 245.1
    text: And when do you need to report the result?
  - startTime: 245.1
    endTime: 246.1
    text: Thank you.
  segments: []
  questions:
  - prompt: Which room should the final poster list?
    answers:
    - Room 201
    - Room 203
    - Room 205
    correctAnswer: 1
    explanation: 
  - prompt: What should you check on the final poster?
    answers:
    - Headline, colors, and logo
    - Workshop capacity and staff arrival time
    - Date, time, room number, and whether the QR code works
    correctAnswer: 2
    explanation: 
  - prompt: When should you report the result to the group?
    answers:
    - Tomorrow by 11 a.m.
    - Tomorrow by noon
    - Tomorrow by 4 p.m.
    correctAnswer: 0
    explanation: 
